# appearance.schema — which layer may decide each key of the `appearance`
# subsystem (Hub -> Appearance -> Settings: per-user overrides that beat the
# active theme).
#
# Read by /usr/lib/w/w-conf-lib.sh during the load pass; see w-conf.md.
#
# All keys are `user`: they tint only the logged-in user's own session (their
# rendered Hyprland config / RGB hardware), so there is no root domain to
# protect — same reasoning as nightlight.schema. No vendor .conf ships for this
# subsystem: the unset default ("follow the active theme") is a plain fallback
# in the reader code, exactly like w-power's per-user idle keys.
#
# Format: <KEY>\t<scope>       scope: system | user | both

# "" (unset) = follow the active theme's effects.conf/motion.conf. "off" =
# forced off regardless of theme.
# RGB (unset) = theme switching recolors RGB devices via the w-style `rgb` axis
# (OpenRGB); "off" = devices are left untouched.
# RGB_LEVEL (unset) = "medium" — which of the theme's three RGB pigments
# (soft/medium/crisp, theme.conf's W_RGB_*) the `rgb` axis pushes to the
# hardware. Read regardless of RGB's on/off state (harmless when off).
# Bar position is NOT here — it already has a
# dedicated override slot in config/bar.json (see w-appearance).
BLUR	user
MOTION	user
RGB	user
RGB_LEVEL	user
